### 2.2 Era-Based Event Files

Events are split into era-specific pools. The engine only loads events for the current era + age range.

```json
// data/events/age_events.json
{
  "age_events": [
    {
      "id": "age_5_first_day",
      "min_age": 4,
      "max_age": 6,
      "life_stage": "child",
      "era": ["modern", "magic", "sci-fi", "ancient"],
      "weight": 3,
      "requires": {"flags": {"school_unlocked": false}},
      "framework": "parent_decision",
      "title": "First day of school",
      "text": "Your parents are talking about school.",
      "choices": [
        {"id": "go", "label": "Go to school", "effects": {"flags": {"school_unlocked": true}}},
        {"id": "refuse", "label": "Refuse", "effects": {"flags": {"refused_school": true}}}
      ],
      "narrate": true
    }
  ]
}
```

### 2.3 Event Frameworks

Reusable logic templates that events reference. New events = just add JSON, no Python changes.

```python
FRAMEWORKS = {
    "parent_decision": {"handler": "handle_parent_decision", "requires": ["parents"]},
    "career_step": {"handler": "handle_career_step", "requires": ["career_tracks"]},
