    "life_milestone": {"handler": "handle_life_milestone", "requires": ["player"]},
    "random_encounter": {"handler": "handle_random_encounter", "requires": []},
}
```

## 3. CAREER CHAIN SYSTEM

### 3.1 Career Chain Definition

Each career is a JSON file with stages. Each stage has requirements, unlocks, effects, and an event.

```json
// data/careers/singer.json
{
  "id": "singer",
  "name": "Singer",
  "era": ["modern", "magic", "sci-fi"],
  "stages": [
    {
      "id": "singer_lessons",
      "name": "Take singing lessons",
      "requirements": {"age": 8, "money": 2},
      "unlocks": ["singer_practice"],
      "effects": {"skill": 1, "money": -1},
      "event_framework": "career_step",
      "event": { ... }
    }
  ],
  "job_list": [
    {
      "id": "singer_job",
      "name": "Local Singer",
      "requirements": {"flags": {"singer_performed": true}},
      "pay": 2, "energy_cost": 1, "skill_gain": 1, "reputation_gain": 1
    }
  ]
}
```

### 3.2 How Career Chains Work

1. Career chains are hidden — no visible job buttons
2. Each stage has requirements (age, skill, money, flags, relationships)
3. When requirements are met, the career step event triggers via Event Director
4. The LLM narrates the event text and shapes choices
5. The framework handler applies state changes
6. Unlocking a stage reveals the next stage's requirements
7. Job listings appear only when the player has unlocked the relevant stage

